  "text": "The drawbacks next: the salt is the real catch. Brining pushes sodium to roughly 1.1 grams per 100 grams, so portions matter even before the saturated fat gets involved. It is still a dairy food. Milk allergy or poor dairy tolerance can rule it out completely. The sharp flavour can take over. Feta works brilliantly as an accent, but it is not always what you want dominating the entire meal.",
